{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00145",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.05,
      "end_seconds": 4.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Right, come in and get settled."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.09,
      "end_seconds": 6.79,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hi."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.88,
      "end_seconds": 11.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Tell me what's been troubling you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.28,
      "end_seconds": 25.16,
      "duration_seconds": 12.88,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got a fever that won't go away. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.37,
      "end_seconds": 29.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "How far back does it go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.5,
      "end_seconds": 34.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Okay, so it's been about two weeks now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.38,
      "end_seconds": 42.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.74,
      "end_seconds": 64.46,
      "duration_seconds": 19.72,
      "text": "It feels mild to me. As for bad headache, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. I've been feeling weak too, you know, for two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.36,
      "end_seconds": 71.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.97,
      "end_seconds": 76.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "So, yes, eggs, it gives me stomach cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.48,
      "end_seconds": 81.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Is there anything medical in your background?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.65,
      "end_seconds": 94.03,
      "duration_seconds": 11.38,
      "text": "Oh, I've got diabetes. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.62,
      "end_seconds": 96.32,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Yes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.33,
      "end_seconds": 103.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.47,
      "text": "I have acid reflux. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.62,
      "end_seconds": 114.63,
      "duration_seconds": 9.01,
      "text": "Hm, okay. Yes, diabetes and acid reflux are known to us, good to have that clear. Have you had any surgery before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.58,
      "end_seconds": 121.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Just a knee arthroscopy, three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.79,
      "end_seconds": 142.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.53,
      "end_seconds": 146.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.89,
      "end_seconds": 150.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "How long have you taken that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.15,
      "end_seconds": 162.83,
      "duration_seconds": 11.68,
      "text": "For nearly five years. I'm on Dolo, 650 milligrams, when I get the fever. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.53,
      "end_seconds": 165.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.66,
      "end_seconds": 167.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "I've never smoked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.91,
      "end_seconds": 169.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.26,
      "end_seconds": 173.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "I don't drink at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.19,
      "end_seconds": 178.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "What kind of work do you do?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.89,
      "end_seconds": 183.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "I work on a farm, it's quite physical."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.47,
      "end_seconds": 186.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Any sport or activity?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.28,
      "end_seconds": 190.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "I play badminton on Sundays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.02,
      "end_seconds": 194.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "And what do you usually eat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.74,
      "end_seconds": 201.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Mostly home-cooked food, rice and vegetables."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.28,
      "end_seconds": 207.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "Have you had any rash or burning when passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.58,
      "end_seconds": 215.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "I haven't had rash or burning when passing urine, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.48,
      "end_seconds": 220.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Any blood in the stool, vomiting or cough at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.08,
      "end_seconds": 230.5,
      "duration_seconds": 8.42,
      "text": "Okay, you know, so I haven't had blood in the stool, vomiting or cough, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.01,
      "end_seconds": 235.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "So, any breathing difficulties apart from this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.91,
      "end_seconds": 237.84,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "Breathing's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 248.61,
      "end_seconds": 258.29,
      "duration_seconds": 9.68,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temp 38.3 degrees, heart rate 102, pressure 106 over 68. SpO2 97 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.63,
      "end_seconds": 260.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.83,
      "end_seconds": 265.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Okay, I need to examine you for this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 267.11,
      "end_seconds": 267.81,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.05,
      "end_seconds": 271.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Let me just check something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.62,
      "end_seconds": 290.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Your tummy is a bit full and tender in the lower part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.25,
      "end_seconds": 293.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Let me just check something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.81,
      "end_seconds": 306.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "I can't feel your liver or spleen enlarged."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.64,
      "end_seconds": 311.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Right, you can sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.59,
      "end_seconds": 352.26,
      "duration_seconds": 31.67,
      "text": "Let me tell you where I've got to. The most likely explanation is typhoid fever, which we need to confirm. I'm going to order a malaria test, for fever. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. We should do blood cultures for prolonged fever. Eat only home-cooked food and drink boiled or bottled water while this is going on. Please take the tablets with food so they don't upset your stomach."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.68,
      "end_seconds": 375.69,
      "duration_seconds": 22.01,
      "text": "Let's hold off on a full blood count for now, and if there's no change in a month we can revisit it. One warning sign to remember: the fever stays high or the tummy pain gets sharp. In that case don't wait. I'd like you back in three days. Thanks for coming in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 377.59,
      "end_seconds": 380.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "One thing: no, actually that's all. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}